course: dictionary
lesson: 2367
title: Cull: one word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Cull has two main meanings, and the words around it show you which one to use. Most often, to cull animals means to kill some of them on purpose, to keep a group small or healthy. «The council agreed to a deer cull after the herd grew too big.»
explain: The second meaning is quite different: to cull means to choose and collect things from many places. «The historian culled facts from old letters and books.» Nobody is killed here. Ask yourself: what would fit in this sentence? Collected would fit, so cull means collect.
explain: Some people choose softer words to make a hard thing sound ordinary. Farmers and officials may say «pest control» or «processed» instead of killing. When you read these words, check what they really mean, and remember that a dictionary can tell you the plain meaning.
fact: Cull can be a verb (to cull, culls, culled, culling) or a noun (a cull, culls).
fact: «Culled» means animals were killed to reduce their numbers, or gathered from many sources, depending on the sentence.
fact: In maths problems, a cull reduces a population, so it is a subtraction.
fact: «A deer cull» is a common phrase in nature news, and people often argue about it.
fact: A noun is a naming word; a cull is an act, so it can be a naming word for that act.
exercise: In a maths problem, a cull reduces a population. Which operation does that suggest? | Add | *Subtract | Multiply | Share equally
exercise: «The historian culled facts from old letters and books.» What does culled mean here? | *Chose and collected from many sources | Printed in colour | Lost forever | Burned to ash
exercise: «The cull was argued about at the council meeting.» What kind of word is cull here? | A verb, an action word | An adjective, a describing word | A full stop | *A noun, a naming word
test: Which sentence uses culled to mean chose and gathered? | «The farmer culled the herd last spring.» | *«She culled the best ideas from her notes.» | «The cull reduced the number of pests.» | «The deer were culled to keep the herd healthy.»
test: Why might an official say «pest control» instead of killing? | Because it is a number | To make it sound like a party | *To make a hard act sound like ordinary work | Because it means feeding animals
exam: «The writer culled ideas from three books.» What does culled mean? | Read aloud | Forgot | *Gathered and chose from many sources | Painted
